## 2. PDF extraction and cleaning

**E1: Page numbers are physical PDF pages, not printed page numbers** · Status: By design
Printed footers (for example "Apple Inc. | Page 43") drift from the physical page because of how EDGAR HTML is converted to PDF, so printed numbers are ignored. "Page 61" in the metadata always means page 61 of the trimmed PDF file, which is the page the viewer opens when a citation is clicked. A citation can therefore differ from the number printed on the page.

**E2: URLs are removed** · Impact: Data (minor) · Status: Deferred
The cleaner removes URLs at the end of the document and inside paragraphs. Questions such as "What is Apple's investor-relations website?" cannot be answered. Such questions are rare.

**E3: Repeating page-header captions (Costco, Item 7)** · Impact: Cosmetic · Tier 2/3 · Status: Open
Captions such as "(In millions ...) (Continued)" remain as small paragraph clutter. Root cause in `paragraph_parser.py`; pending raw JSON verification.

