## 3. Heading detection and hierarchy

**H1: Heading detection is visual (font-based), not semantic** · Impact: Structure · Status: Accepted
In narrative sections, sub-topics styled like body text or like their siblings are not detected as headings (Apple FY2016 Item 1: "iOS", "macOS", "Services"); their text is absorbed into the nearest parent heading. No data loss. Audit: 13 level-4 heading clusters in Apple FY2016; only 1 ("Products", p. 5) affected.

**H2: Apple FY2021, Item 7 (MD&A) heading not detected** · Impact: Structure · Tier 1/2 · Status: Open
In FY2016 Item 7 had 25 children. In FY2021 the Item 7 heading was not detected and the MD&A content (products, segments, iPhone sales ...) sits under "Item 6. [Reserved]" (9 children), probably because of different line wrapping or spacing in that PDF. These chunks carry "Item 6. [Reserved]" as their section, which is misleading in citations and for questions such as "What does Apple's MD&A say ...".

**H3: Oversized sub-headings flatten the tree (Intel FY2025, Palo Alto Networks FY2025)** · Impact: Structure · Status: Open (observing)
Newer 10-K styling uses large fonts for sub-headings, which become level-1 nodes (for example Item 8 → Notes, Audit Report → Critical Audit Matters). Direct questions are unaffected; requests for a whole subtree (all children of Item 8) may return partial results. A layout-aware rule will be added after more samples, to avoid over-segmentation.

**H4: Titles split across nodes or left blank** · Impact: Cosmetic / Structure · Status: Deferred
- Ametek FY2016: titles of Items 1, 1A, 2, 3 and 5 wrap into a separate child node (formerly #35).
- eBay FY2016: titles of Items 5, 7, 9, 12 and 13 wrap into separate child nodes (no item-title continuation logic).
- Kimberly-Clark FY2016 and FY2025: the ITEM 8 node has a blank title (title continuation not merged); it still works as the parent.
- Nike FY2025: the Shareholders' Equity statement title is cut to "CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF" (the title wraps over more than two lines); data intact.
- Meta FY2025: a two-column Critical Audit Matter title splits into "Description of the" / "Matter" (two empty nodes).
- PayPal FY2025: the Item 16 exhibit-listing sentence splits into two small headings ("Consolidated Statements of Income (Loss), (iii) the Consolidated" / "... Stockholders' Equity, (v) the"); boilerplate only.

**H5: Captions and dividers promoted to child headings** · Impact: Cosmetic / Structure · Status: Deferred
- Emerson FY2016 and FY2025: "EMERSON ELECTRIC CO. & SUBSIDIARIES" becomes a child heading under all five core statements (same pattern as Union Pacific).
- Union Pacific FY2025: "Millions, except share and per share amounts ..." under the Balance Sheet; "Union Pacific Corporation and Subsidiary Companies" under the Cash Flow statement.
- Rockwell Automation FY2016 and FY2025: the "Liabilities and Shareowners' Equity" divider forms its own empty node, so the Balance Sheet is split across two sibling nodes; values are complete (Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity in both years) (formerly #31).

The retriever's statement detector checks the parent heading when the last heading is such a caption, so these statements are still recognised.

**H6: Spurious or merged nodes** · Impact: Cosmetic · Status: Deferred
- Intuit: stock-performance chart legends ("S&P 500", "S&P 500 Information Technology Index") create empty heading nodes.
- PayPal FY2016: the signature blocks of two directors (Wences Casares, John J. Donahoe) sit under one concatenated heading.

**H7: Emerson "ITEM 6 [RESERVED]" not matched as an Item marker** · Impact: None (the section is empty) · Status: Deferred
The bracketed format without trailing punctuation bypasses the `is_top_level_marker` regex.

**H8: Wrong parent headings found during the retrieval evaluation** · Status: Open
See R1 (Colgate-Palmolive, Watts Water, Block, Alphabet, Parker Hannifin, Chevron) and R3 (Caterpillar FY2016 cash-flow statement).

**H9: Resolved (kept for regression tracking)**
- AMD FY2025: a cash-flow statement repeated over page breaks without "(Continued)" created duplicate sibling nodes; fixed with node-reopening logic in `hierarchy_builder.py`.
- Rockwell Automation FY2016: the Item 5 heading was not recognised (its title exceeded a length threshold); fixed, and Items 4A / 5 / 6 now nest correctly.

